    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\( x \\cdot (x + y) = x^2 + 8 \\) and find the value of \\( xy \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Expand the left-hand side of the equation:**\n   \\[\n   x \\cdot (x + y) = x^2 + xy\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   x^2 + xy = x^2 + 8\n   \\]\n\n2. **Subtract \\( x^2 \\) from both sides of the equation:**\n   \\[\n   x^2 + xy - x^2 = x^2 + 8 - x^2\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   xy = 8\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the value of \\( xy \\):**\n   From the equation \\( xy = 8 \\), we can see that the value of \\( xy \\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{8}\n   \\]",
